From a40d1495ba0d2a61bfe1fb946da3f47e1f4c1efb Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Rowland <simon@simonrowland.com>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 00:13:31 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Keep the four-cation scaling in the sb FeO activity

compute_activities() set G0_fper from the sb wustite end member and
divided by 4 for EM_database 1 and 2 (sb21 and sb24, where wu is
Fe4O4). The next statement then stored PP_db.gbase unconditionally.
That second store is what made the tc path use fper at all: fper is
one FeO, and the tc branch never assigned gbase itself. It also
threw away the sb /4.

The tc branch now stores PP_db.gbase inside the branch, with no /4.
The unconditional store is removed. The sb /4 for EM_database 1 and
2 is unchanged. sb11 wu is one FeO (EM_database 0), so that path
does not divide and its activity is unchanged. The later Fe+O block
is not part of this change.

Repro on v1.9.6 with the periclase-reference fix already applied.
R = 0.0083144 kJ/mol/K. Printed Gamma and gbase are kJ.

sb21, --Temp=1600 C (1873.15 K), --Pres=100 kbar, --sys_in=mol,
    --Bulk=38,3,2,8,48,1 (SiO2 CaO Al2O3 FeO MgO Na2O). The mw end
members are pe, wu, anao and the wu row is Fe = 4.
G_wu = -1246.65837 kJ, Gamma_FeO = -323.30963 kJ.
  before aFeO = 5.599946e+25 = exp((Gamma_FeO - G_wu)/RT)
  after  aFeO = 4.734460e-01 = exp((Gamma_FeO - G_wu/4)/RT)
  relative difference of the printed value from that exponential
  is -1.3e-07
  assemblage unchanged: ol 0.71429, gtmj 0.09292, cpx 0.19280,
  17 iterations, status 0. aSiO2, aAl2O3 and aMgO unchanged.

sb11, same bulk, --Temp=1400 C, --Pres=20 kbar. wu is Fe = 1.
aFeO = 1.893221e-01 before and after, which is
exp((Gamma_FeO - G_wu)/RT) and not G_wu/4.
23 iterations, ol + cpx + sp, unchanged.

ig, --Temp=1599.85 C, --buffer=qfm --buffer_n=-3.205734. Kume 2000
sample 305 and the MgO-50 sanity bulk, at 1e-6 bar and at 1 bar:
aFeO, aMgO, aSiO2, aAl2O3, phase list, mole modes and iteration
count are identical to the binary without this change.
---
 src/toolkit.c | 5 ++++-
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/toolkit.c b/src/toolkit.c
index 49281e4..48f66b3 100644
--- a/src/toolkit.c
+++ b/src/toolkit.c
@@ -2026,6 +2026,10 @@ global_variable compute_activities(			int					 EM_database,
 		double G0_fper  = 0.0;
 		if (strcmp(gv.research_group, "tc") 	== 0 ){
 			PP_db  			= G_EM_function(gv.research_group, gv.EM_dataset, gv.len_ox,z_b.id,z_b.bulk_rock, z_b.apo, z_b.P, z_b.T , "fper", "equilibrium");
+			/* fper is one FeO, so tc stores gbase with no /4.
+			   The sb branch scales the 4-cation wu end member.
+			   Assigning gbase again after the branch discarded that /4. */
+			G0_fper 		= PP_db.gbase;
 		}
 		else if (strcmp(gv.research_group, "sb") 	== 0 ){
 			PP_db  			= G_EM_function(gv.research_group, gv.EM_dataset, gv.len_ox,z_b.id,z_b.bulk_rock, z_b.apo, z_b.P, z_b.T , "wu", "equilibrium");
@@ -2034,7 +2038,6 @@ global_variable compute_activities(			int					 EM_database,
 				G0_fper /= 4.0;
 			}
 		}
-		G0_fper  		= PP_db.gbase;//*PP_db.factor;
 		gv.system_aFeO  = exp( (gv.gam_tot[FeO_ix] - G0_fper) / (z_b.R*z_b.T));
 	}
 
